  "value_dedup": "three keys bound to one value: the value is one object, but every key still occupies an address, so this segment reports keys, distinct values and key reduction separately",
  "same_value_containment": "a longer key is dropped only when a shorter key of the SAME value occurs contiguously inside it and no other record's whole key sits inside the longer key outside the kept span",
  "residual_guard": "the guard refuses the drop when another key (any value) is entirely inside the longer key but outside the kept span; the unguarded simulation is reported to show what it prevented",
  "boundary_leak": "a key that straddles the boundary of the dropped wording is not inside it, so the guard passes; the read then answers one extra value -- this is the measured blind spot",
  "cross_value": "containment across different values is excluded by rule; compressing there would answer the short key's value for a query written as the long key's wording",
