  "boundary_leak": "the drop happens (3 -> 2 records) and the read answers both values, including the value that the dropped wording was meant to cover -- the guard is table-local, not query-universal",
  "cross_value": "no record is removed, the cross-value pair is listed, and the hypothetical drop would answer the short key's value -- therefore the same-value condition is required",
  "default_path": "zero records removed, content digest unchanged, regression 40/40 with wrong 0, zeros 0/0",
  "closed_state": "the nine closed-state readings stay equal before and after",
